# Forensa - Environment Variables Example
#
# Copy this file to `.env` in the same directory and fill in the real values.
# `.env` is gitignored. NEVER commit `.env`.
# Pattern adopted from AuditEx (Hack0014) per claude-memory CLAUDE_RULES env-var convention.
#
# Setup steps:
#   1. cp .env.example .env       (PowerShell: Copy-Item .env.example .env)
#   2. Edit .env, replace each `your_*_here` placeholder with a real value.
#   3. Restart your shell so the new env vars are picked up.
#   4. Verify with:   echo $env:FORENSA_GEMINI_API_KEY   (PowerShell)
#   5. If a value is missing, the matching feature falls back to its Mock implementation;
#      see apps/api/main.py for the env-var-to-client wiring (CP9.4).
#
# Optional in dev; REQUIRED for the live narrative demo (CP9.5 MP4 recording).

# === Narrative client (LiveNarrativeClient vs MockNarrativeClient) ===
# Google AI Studio API key for Gemini Pro. Create at https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
# When set: LiveNarrativeClient is wired into apps/api/main.py.
# When unset or empty: MockNarrativeClient is wired (deterministic template; no network).
FORENSA_GEMINI_API_KEY=your_gemini_api_key_here

# Gemini model id to use. Default is gemini-1.5-pro-latest.
# Other valid values: gemini-2.0-flash-exp, gemini-1.5-flash-latest, gemini-1.5-pro-002.
# Note: production Vertex AI deploy will use a different model id namespace; see backlog NEW-P13.X.vertex-migration.
FORENSA_GEMINI_MODEL_ID=gemini-1.5-pro-latest

# === Database ===
# Async DSN; SQLAlchemy 2.0 + asyncpg driver. Default below assumes local docker-compose postgres.
FORENSA_DB_URL=postgresql+asyncpg://forensa:forensa_dev_pw@localhost:5432/forensa

# === Logging / runtime ===
ENVIRONMENT=development
LOG_LEVEL=INFO
API_PORT=8000

# === Reserved for Phase 10+ (do not need to set today) ===
# Auth (Phase 10 CP10.1 OIDC): FORENSA_OIDC_ISSUER_URL, FORENSA_OIDC_CLIENT_ID, FORENSA_OIDC_CLIENT_SECRET
# KMS (Phase 11 CP11.1 HSM): FORENSA_KMS_PROVIDER, FORENSA_KMS_KEY_ID, FORENSA_KMS_REGION
# Vault (Phase 10 CP10.6): FORENSA_VAULT_ADDR, FORENSA_VAULT_TOKEN
# Kafka (Phase 12 CP12.4): FORENSA_KAFKA_BROKERS, FORENSA_KAFKA_TOPIC
